{title: Frames of the Tabernacle}
{subtitle: Exodus 6:19; Numbers 3:20–33; 4:29–33; 26:58; 1 Chronicles 6:19–29; 23:21–23}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The sons of Merari, Mahli and Mushi stood
Founders of the clan, by [Gm]the Lord understood
In the wilderness [Gm7]camp, behind [Eb]the holy tent
The Mah[Bb]lites prepared where the co[F]venant went
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Carrying the [Bb]frames, the posts and the bases too
The ropes and the pegs, the work assigned to you
[Gm]From thirty to fifty, strong for [Eb]the task
Serving the sanctuary, the [Bb]sacred place
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The census was taken, every male named
Recorded in Numbers, in history [Gm]claimed
Eleazar and Kish, the lineage flowed [Eb]on
In David's tem[Bb]ple, the service [F]was done
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Carrying [Bb]the frames, the posts and the bases too
The ropes and the pegs, the work assigned to you
[Gm]From thirty to fifty, strong for [Eb]the task
Serving the sanctuary, the [Bb]sacred place
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
No sons remained, but cousins took [Gm]hold
Married the daugh[Eb]ters, the story is [Bb]told
The Mashites joined, the line kept in[Gm]tact
Faithful [Eb]in service, standing [F]firm
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Carrying the frames, the posts and [Bb]the bases too
The ropes and the pegs, the work assigned to you
[Gm]From thirty to fifty, strong for [Eb]the task
Serving the sanctuary, the [Bb]sacred place
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Mahli, son of Merari, Levi's line
Preserved the ta[Gm]bernacle, holy and divine
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
